{"name":"Arabian Red","hex":"#a14c3f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arabian Peninsula","blocks":[{"text":"The Arabian Peninsula, or simply Arabia, is a peninsula in West Asia. It accounts for the majority of the land situated on the Arabian plate. With an area of 3,237,500 km2 (1.25 million mi2), it is the world's largest peninsula—roughly comparable in size to India. Nine countries are located on the Arabian Peninsula: Bahrain, Kuwait, Oman, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, and Yemen, as well as the southern halves of Iraq and Jordan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Arabian_Peninsula_dust_SeaWiFS.jpg/330px-Arabian_Peninsula_dust_SeaWiFS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arabian_Peninsula","wikidata":"Q31945"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Near_East_in_1000bc_%28en%29.jpg/500px-Near_East_in_1000bc_%28en%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Near_East_in_1000bc_%28en%29.jpg/500px-Near_East_in_1000bc_%28en%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pre-Islamic Arabia in 1000 BC","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANear_East_in_1000bc_(en).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Umayyad750ADloc.png/500px-Umayyad750ADloc.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Umayyad750ADloc.png/1280px-Umayyad750ADloc.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Umayyad750ADloc.png/500px-Umayyad750ADloc.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Umayyad Caliphate (661–750)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUmayyad750ADloc.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Ayyubid.png/500px-Ayyubid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Ayyubid.png/500px-Ayyubid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Middle East, c. 1190. Saladin's empire and its vassals shown in red","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAyyubid.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Persian_Gulf_z1507-1750.gif/5